  %% ESP32-WROOM-32E GPIO assignments, mirroring the board's edge connectors.
  %% Pumps run on two on-board DRV8870 H-bridges; the sensor loom and relays land
  %% on the SENSORS / RELAYS connectors. The six inputs sit on input-only /
  %% boot-safe pads.
  %% Valves + reeds ride the MCP23017 expanders (MCP -> TBD62083), not direct GPIO.
  %% Current plan:
  %%   GPIO 19 drives the Teyleten relay #1 (compressor AC).
  %%   GPIO 2 drives the Teyleten relay #2 (diaphragm pump 12 V, refill) — boot-safe:
  %%     the opto module's LED load holds it low, which download mode also wants.
  %%   GPIO 26 hosts the 1-wire temp bus: DS18B20 (0x28, tank-wall) + DS18S20 (0x10, evap-suction), told apart by family code.
  %%   GPIO 25 reads the DIGITEN flow meter (pulse input).
  %%   GPIO 27 reads the backflow drip-pan moisture sensor (SIG-9).
  %%   GPIO 23 sources the moisture module's VCC (switched: driven only while sampling,
  %%     so the always-wet drip-pan electrodes sit unpowered between samples — no
  %%     electrolytic corrosion from a continuously energized probe).
  %%   GPIO 13 drives the on-board buzzer (U8 magnetic transducer, PWM tone via
  %%     LEDC, low-side switched by Q1).
  %%   GPIO 39 reads the MQ-6 gas / refrigerant-leak sensor AOUT (analog, ADC1) and
  %%     GPIO 36 reads its DOUT (LM393 comparator trip). MQ-6 outputs swing 0-5 V,
  %%     divided to 3.3 V on-board (36/39 are not 5 V tolerant). DOUT is the
  %%     hardware gas-trip signal (sensor low on the rear cabinet floor).
  %%   Pumps: two on-board DRV8870 H-bridges, single-direction drive — A IN1 on
  %%     GPIO 17 (U11), B IN1 on GPIO 4 (U12); each IN2 is tied to GND on-board
  %%     (peristaltic tubing occlusion stops backflow, so no reverse).
  %% All 10 reed switches — 8 flavor-reservoir (4 per reservoir) + 2 carbonator
  %% (low/high) — are read through the I2C MCP23017 expanders, not direct ESP32
  %% GPIO, so every reed rides the MCP internal pull-up (no external resistors):
  %%   MCP23017 0x20: 8 valves (V-A..V-H) on PA[0:7] -> ULN U4 -> MANIFOLD A
  %%     (silk-up ULN reverses the bank: GPA0->V-H .. GPA7->V-A);
  %%     Rsvr A 4 reeds on PB[0:3]; PB[4:7] spare.
  %%   MCP23017 0x21: 3 valves (V-I/V-J + V-K water supply) + condenser fan on
  %%     PA -> ULN U5 -> MANIFOLD B (PA5 drives J2.OUT3 → V-K; PA4 drives J2.OUT4,
  %%     wired but carrying no valve — spare capacity); Rsvr B 4 reeds on PB[0:3];
  %%     carbonator reeds low/high on PB[4:5]; spares elsewhere. See
  %%     valve-control.mmd.
  %% Also on the I2C bus: an off-board MPR121 cap-sense controller (0x5A) reads
  %%   copper-foil ring electrodes on the flavor tubes (fluid-in-line detection) —
  %%   it plugs into the on-board J8 I2C header (GND/3V3/SDA/SCL, all plane nets), no
  %%   ESP GPIO. See hardware/printed-parts/flavor/cap-sense-sleeve.
  %% Two display UARTs:
  %%   GPIO 32/34 = Serial1 -> ALMOCN RS485 transceiver -> 4.3B config display
  %%                (front panel, internal run; the 4.3B has no free TTL UART).
  %%   GPIO 33/35 = Serial2, direct TTL UART -> 1.47" faucet display
  %%                (up the umbilical; the 1.47" breaks out TTL UART).
  %%   On-board status LEDs (active-high to GND, boot-safe), flanking the brand logo:
  %%     RED on 15 (fault; high during boot — a glint at reset), GREEN on 12 (ready),
  %%     BLUE on 14 (activity); 3V3 + 5V rail greens light straight off their planes
  %%     (no GPIO).
  %% Free GPIOs:
  %%   GPIO 5   - free (bootstrap-sensitive; high at boot)
  %%   GPIO 16  - free
  %%   GPIO 18  - free
  %% Programming — on-board USB-C block (J14 receptacle + U13 CH340C USB-UART bridge):
  %%   GPIO 0   boot strap (R8 pull-up to 3V3, BOOT button, DTR auto-reset via Q3)
  %%   GPIO 1   U0TXD (-> CH340 RXD)
  %%   GPIO 3   U0RXD (-> CH340 TXD)
  %%   EN       reset (R7/C12 RC, RESET button, RTS auto-reset via Q2)

  subgraph ESP["ESP32-WROOM-32E"]
    direction TB

    subgraph UART_Pins["UART  (displays)"]
